1Analyses were analyzed by study.  Each study inverse normalized the trait by sex and case status if applicable.  Analyses were adjusted for age and principle components 1-10, and study specific covariates.   Waist to hip ratio trait was also adjusted for BMI. All studies were meta-analyzed using METAL (Willer et al 2010; PMID 20616382)																									
2BMI analyses did not include Brazilians or American Indians. WHRadjBMI analyses did not include Brazilians (American Indian samples did not have this trait).																									
3This study was based on the FINDOR method (Kichaev et al 2018 PMID: 30595370).  Beta and standard errors are from the UK Biobank, European ancestry.																									
